1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:06,090
Pure green: 255 becomes 215.

2
00:00:06,090 --> 00:00:11,590
The label, or the pixels?

3
00:00:11,590 --> 00:00:16,260
Reader 1: the label.

4
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:20,930
Reader 2: the pixels.

5
00:00:20,930 --> 00:00:23,270
ffmpeg 6.1.1.

6
00:00:23,270 --> 00:00:28,590
Plain: no tag, BT.601 pixels.

7
00:00:28,590 --> 00:00:36,040
Read as BT.709: green 255 to 215.

8
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:41,360
-colorspace bt709 alone: error 40.

9
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:47,920
Default: black Y 16, white Y 235.

10
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:51,670
-color_range pc: same bytes.

11
00:00:51,670 --> 00:00:57,300
Tag says full: black shows 16.

12
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:07,040
100 nit white lands at Y 127.

13
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:13,990
iall=bt2020: same pixels, new tags.

14
00:01:13,990 --> 00:01:19,580
3 commands changed only the label.

15
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:23,310
A wrong label: fixable.

16
00:01:23,310 --> 00:01:28,600
yuv420p: red line becomes 150, 21, 149.

17
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:35,410
Y stays near 81. No tag brings it back.

18
00:01:35,410 --> 00:01:41,520
format=yuv420p: 65 values, not 64.

19
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:45,190
Only sws_dither=none truncates.

20
00:01:45,190 --> 00:01:51,300
6 other spellings: 1 checksum.

21
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:57,240
BT.709 file: format=gray gives 183.

22
00:01:57,240 --> 00:02:04,360
601 mixer: 149. 34 levels off.

23
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:08,950
ffprobe: bt709, tv.

24
00:02:08,950 --> 00:02:15,070
Decoded: worst error 1.

25
00:02:15,070 --> 00:02:21,180
Black 16, white 235.

26
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:27,300
Plain command: error 40.

27
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:32,220
Check the label and the pixels.

28
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:36,320
Not tested: footage, players, HLG.
